<article class="env-example" id="0EV1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EV1">Example <span data-tag="0EV1">38.35.2</span>.</a> On any of the sites $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_ h$ the topology is not subcanonical, in other words, representable sheaves are not sheaves. Namely, the “structure sheaf” $\mathcal{O}$ is representable because $\mathcal{O}(X) = \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _ S(X, \mathbf{A}^1_ S)$ in $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_ h$ and we saw in Example <a href="/tag/0EV0" data-tag="0EV0">38.35.1</a> that $\mathcal{O}$ is not a sheaf. </p>
</article>